      ],
      "extract": "This paper is concerned with two invariants for a 3-manifold with torus boundary. The ﬁrst is geometric. If the interior of the 3-manifold admits a hyperbolic structure, then a tubular neighborhood of the torus boundary inherits a Euclidean structure, and this Euclidean structure is unique up to similarity of the torus. The similarity class of such a Euclidean structure is called the cusp shape of the 3-manifold.",
      "extractCut": true
